√śram (śrā́myati [763]; śaśrā́ma; áśramīt;
śrāntá; -śrámya). be weary;
take pains; esp. castigate one's self,
96^10.
[]
+ ā, in āśrama, ‘hermitage.’
+ pari, weary one's self exceedingly;
pariśrānta, tired of, disgusted with.

śrávaṇa,
 —1. m. ear;
 —2. n. hearing;
--3. n. fame. [√śru, 1150. 1a: for mg 3,
cf. śravas and esp. under √śru.]

√śrā or śrī or śṛ or śir (śrīṇā́ti, śrīṇīté;
śiśriyé; śrātá, śrītá, śṛtá, śīrtá). cook;
boil; śṛtá, cooked, done.
